{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some models expose their internal reasoning as \"thinking\" content -- Claude with extended thinking, OpenAI o-series models with reasoning, and others. TanStack AI captures this as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" in messages, streamed to your UI in real-time alongside text and tool calls."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unsigned thinking stays in the UI. Signed thinking is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signature"},{"type":"text","value":". Anthropic extended thinking uses this. The next request sends signed thinking back in the same order as the original response, including around provider-executed tools. The next-turn body puts that signature on spec "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"encryptedValue"},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: \"reasoning\""},{"type":"text","value":" fan-out. Stream events use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-it-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How It Works"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message.parts"},{"type":"text","value":". Thinking content comes from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_*"},{"type":"text","value":" events and from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" only carry "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stepName"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n  stepId?: string;\n  signature?: string;\n  redacted?: boolean;\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" appears in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage.parts"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCallPart"},{"type":"text","value":" entries. As reasoning tokens arrive, its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" accumulates token by token."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude can also send a redacted thinking block. It is encrypted, so it has no text. It arrives as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redacted: true"},{"type":"text","value":", an empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", and the encrypted data in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signature"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep the part in your stored messages: the next request sends it back to Claude unchanged. In a UI, show a short placeholder such as \"Thinking hidden\" instead of the empty text."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"enabling-thinking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enabling Thinking"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How you enable thinking depends on the provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"anthropic-extended-thinking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic (Extended Thinking)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinking"},{"type":"text","value":" option in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: \"enabled\""},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"budget_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" (minimum 1024). Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"budget_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" below "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" so there is room for the visible response in addition to the thinking budget:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { anthropicText } from \"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      max_tokens: 32000,\n      // budget_tokens must be at least 1024 and below max_tokens\n      thinking: { type: \"enabled\", budget_tokens: 10000 },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai-reasoning-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI (Reasoning Models)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI o-series models (o1, o3, o3-mini, o3-pro) perform reasoning automatically. You can control the depth with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"o3-mini\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: {\n        effort: \"medium\", // 'none' | 'minimal' | 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'\n        summary: \"auto\", // 'auto' | 'detailed'\n      },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reasoning.summary"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, the adapter streams reasoning summary text as thinking content. Without it, reasoning tokens are still used internally but may not be surfaced depending on the model."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GPT-5 and later models also support reasoning. Their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reasoning.effort"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\""},{"type":"text","value":", and reasoning activates on any non-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"none"},{"type":"text","value":" value:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: { effort: \"high\" },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-in-react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering in React"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking parts appear in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message.parts"},{"type":"text","value":" just like text and tool calls. A common pattern is to render them in a collapsible element so they don't dominate the UI:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction MessageContent({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {message.parts.map((part, idx) => {\n        if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n          return (\n            <details key={idx}>\n              <summary>Thinking...</summary>\n              <pre style={{ whiteSpace: \"pre-wrap\" }}>{part.content}</pre>\n            </details>\n          );\n        }\n        if (part.type === \"text\") {\n          return <p key={idx}>{part.content}</p>;\n        }\n        return null;\n      })}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"streaming-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking content streams "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"before"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the final text response. As reasoning tokens arrive, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart.content"},{"type":"text","value":" accumulates token by token, the same way "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart.content"},{"type":"text","value":" does for the response text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The typical streaming order is:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning starts ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_START"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_MESSAGE_START"},{"type":"text","value":"). Encrypted blobs use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning tokens stream in ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":") and accumulate into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart.content"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_START"},{"type":"text","value":" starts the visible response."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT"},{"type":"text","value":" streams the response text."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" only carry "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stepName"},{"type":"text","value":". They do not carry thinking text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the Solid/Vue/Svelte equivalents), your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" array updates with both thinking and text parts as they arrive."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Connection adapters and stream events"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./agentic-cycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agentic Cycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- How thinking interacts with tool-calling loops"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/anthropic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Full Anthropic provider options"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Full OpenAI provider options"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"how-it-works","text":"How It Works","level":2},{"id":"enabling-thinking","text":"Enabling Thinking","level":2},{"id":"anthropic-extended-thinking","text":"Anthropic (Extended Thinking)","level":3},{"id":"openai-reasoning-models","text":"OpenAI (Reasoning Models)","level":3},{"id":"rendering-in-react","text":"Rendering in React","level":2},{"id":"streaming-behavior","text":"Streaming Behavior","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSome models expose their internal reasoning as \"thinking\" content -- Claude with extended thinking, OpenAI o-series models with reasoning, and others. TanStack AI captures this as `ThinkingPart` in messages, streamed to your UI in real-time alongside text and tool calls.\n\nUnsigned thinking stays in the UI. Signed thinking is a `ThinkingPart` with a `signature`. Anthropic extended thinking uses this. The next request sends signed thinking back in the same order as the original response, including around provider-executed tools. The next-turn body puts that signature on spec `encryptedValue` on the `role: \"reasoning\"` fan-out. Stream events use `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`.\n\n## How It Works\n\nRead the `ThinkingPart` in `message.parts`. Thinking content comes from `REASONING_*` events and from `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`. `STEP_STARTED` and `STEP_FINISHED` only carry `stepName`.\n\n```typescript\ninterface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n  stepId?: string;\n  signature?: string;\n  redacted?: boolean;\n}\n```\n\nThe `ThinkingPart` appears in `UIMessage.parts` alongside `TextPart` and `ToolCallPart` entries. As reasoning tokens arrive, its `content` accumulates token by token.\n\nClaude can also send a redacted thinking block. It is encrypted, so it has no text. It arrives as a `ThinkingPart` with `redacted: true`, an empty `content`, and the encrypted data in `signature`. Keep the part in your stored messages: the next request sends it back to Claude unchanged. In a UI, show a short placeholder such as \"Thinking hidden\" instead of the empty text.\n\n## Enabling Thinking\n\nHow you enable thinking depends on the provider.\n\n### Anthropic (Extended Thinking)\n\nPass the `thinking` option in `modelOptions` with `type: \"enabled\"` and a `budget_tokens` (minimum 1024). Keep `budget_tokens` below `modelOptions.max_tokens` so there is room for the visible response in addition to the thinking budget:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { anthropicText } from \"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      max_tokens: 32000,\n      // budget_tokens must be at least 1024 and below max_tokens\n      thinking: { type: \"enabled\", budget_tokens: 10000 },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n### OpenAI (Reasoning Models)\n\nOpenAI o-series models (o1, o3, o3-mini, o3-pro) perform reasoning automatically. You can control the depth with the `reasoning` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"o3-mini\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: {\n        effort: \"medium\", // 'none' | 'minimal' | 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'\n        summary: \"auto\", // 'auto' | 'detailed'\n      },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nWhen `reasoning.summary` is set, the adapter streams reasoning summary text as thinking content. Without it, reasoning tokens are still used internally but may not be surfaced depending on the model.\n\nGPT-5 and later models also support reasoning. Their `reasoning.effort` accepts `\"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"`, and reasoning activates on any non-`none` value:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: { effort: \"high\" },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Rendering in React\n\nThinking parts appear in `message.parts` just like text and tool calls. A common pattern is to render them in a collapsible element so they don't dominate the UI:\n\n```tsx\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction MessageContent({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {message.parts.map((part, idx) => {\n        if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n          return (\n            <details key={idx}>\n              <summary>Thinking...</summary>\n              <pre style={{ whiteSpace: \"pre-wrap\" }}>{part.content}</pre>\n            </details>\n          );\n        }\n        if (part.type === \"text\") {\n          return <p key={idx}>{part.content}</p>;\n        }\n        return null;\n      })}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Streaming Behavior\n\nThinking content streams **before** the final text response. As reasoning tokens arrive, `ThinkingPart.content` accumulates token by token, the same way `TextPart.content` does for the response text.\n\nThe typical streaming order is:\n\n1. Reasoning starts (`REASONING_START` / `REASONING_MESSAGE_START`). Encrypted blobs use `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`.\n2. Reasoning tokens stream in (`REASONING_MESSAGE_CONTENT`) and accumulate into `ThinkingPart.content`.\n3. `TEXT_MESSAGE_START` starts the visible response.\n4. `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` streams the response text.\n\n`STEP_STARTED` and `STEP_FINISHED` only carry `stepName`. They do not carry thinking text.\n\nIf you use `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-react` (or the Solid/Vue/Svelte equivalents), your `messages` array updates with both thinking and text parts as they arrive.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Streaming](./streaming) -- Connection adapters and stream events\n- [Agentic Cycle](./agentic-cycle) -- How thinking interacts with tool-calling loops\n- [Anthropic Adapter](../adapters/anthropic) -- Full Anthropic provider options\n- [OpenAI Adapter](../adapters/openai) -- Full OpenAI provider options\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Thinking & Reasoning\nid: thinking-content\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Render reasoning tokens from thinking models (Claude extended thinking, OpenAI o-series) as streamed ThinkingPart in TanStack AI chat UIs.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - thinking\n  - reasoning\n  - extended thinking\n  - claude thinking\n  - o-series\n  - chain of thought\n  - ThinkingPart\n---\n\nSome models expose their internal reasoning as \"thinking\" content -- Claude with extended thinking, OpenAI o-series models with reasoning, and others. TanStack AI captures this as `ThinkingPart` in messages, streamed to your UI in real-time alongside text and tool calls.\n\nUnsigned thinking stays in the UI. Signed thinking is a `ThinkingPart` with a `signature`. Anthropic extended thinking uses this. The next request sends signed thinking back in the same order as the original response, including around provider-executed tools. The next-turn body puts that signature on spec `encryptedValue` on the `role: \"reasoning\"` fan-out. Stream events use `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`.\n\n## How It Works\n\nRead the `ThinkingPart` in `message.parts`. Thinking content comes from `REASONING_*` events and from `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`. `STEP_STARTED` and `STEP_FINISHED` only carry `stepName`.\n\n```typescript\ninterface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n  stepId?: string;\n  signature?: string;\n  redacted?: boolean;\n}\n```\n\nThe `ThinkingPart` appears in `UIMessage.parts` alongside `TextPart` and `ToolCallPart` entries. As reasoning tokens arrive, its `content` accumulates token by token.\n\nClaude can also send a redacted thinking block. It is encrypted, so it has no text. It arrives as a `ThinkingPart` with `redacted: true`, an empty `content`, and the encrypted data in `signature`. Keep the part in your stored messages: the next request sends it back to Claude unchanged. In a UI, show a short placeholder such as \"Thinking hidden\" instead of the empty text.\n\n## Enabling Thinking\n\nHow you enable thinking depends on the provider.\n\n### Anthropic (Extended Thinking)\n\nPass the `thinking` option in `modelOptions` with `type: \"enabled\"` and a `budget_tokens` (minimum 1024). Keep `budget_tokens` below `modelOptions.max_tokens` so there is room for the visible response in addition to the thinking budget:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { anthropicText } from \"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      max_tokens: 32000,\n      // budget_tokens must be at least 1024 and below max_tokens\n      thinking: { type: \"enabled\", budget_tokens: 10000 },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n### OpenAI (Reasoning Models)\n\nOpenAI o-series models (o1, o3, o3-mini, o3-pro) perform reasoning automatically. You can control the depth with the `reasoning` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"o3-mini\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: {\n        effort: \"medium\", // 'none' | 'minimal' | 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'\n        summary: \"auto\", // 'auto' | 'detailed'\n      },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nWhen `reasoning.summary` is set, the adapter streams reasoning summary text as thinking content. Without it, reasoning tokens are still used internally but may not be surfaced depending on the model.\n\nGPT-5 and later models also support reasoning. Their `reasoning.effort` accepts `\"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"`, and reasoning activates on any non-`none` value:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      reasoning: { effort: \"high\" },\n    },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Rendering in React\n\nThinking parts appear in `message.parts` just like text and tool calls. A common pattern is to render them in a collapsible element so they don't dominate the UI:\n\n```tsx\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction MessageContent({ message }: { message: UIMessage }) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {message.parts.map((part, idx) => {\n        if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n          return (\n            <details key={idx}>\n              <summary>Thinking...</summary>\n              <pre style={{ whiteSpace: \"pre-wrap\" }}>{part.content}</pre>\n            </details>\n          );\n        }\n        if (part.type === \"text\") {\n          return <p key={idx}>{part.content}</p>;\n        }\n        return null;\n      })}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Streaming Behavior\n\nThinking content streams **before** the final text response. As reasoning tokens arrive, `ThinkingPart.content` accumulates token by token, the same way `TextPart.content` does for the response text.\n\nThe typical streaming order is:\n\n1. Reasoning starts (`REASONING_START` / `REASONING_MESSAGE_START`). Encrypted blobs use `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`.\n2. Reasoning tokens stream in (`REASONING_MESSAGE_CONTENT`) and accumulate into `ThinkingPart.content`.\n3. `TEXT_MESSAGE_START` starts the visible response.\n4. `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` streams the response text.\n\n`STEP_STARTED` and `STEP_FINISHED` only carry `stepName`. They do not carry thinking text.\n\nIf you use `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-react` (or the Solid/Vue/Svelte equivalents), your `messages` array updates with both thinking and text parts as they arrive.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Streaming](./streaming) -- Connection adapters and stream events\n- [Agentic Cycle](./agentic-cycle) -- How thinking interacts with tool-calling loops\n- [Anthropic Adapter](../adapters/anthropic) -- Full Anthropic provider options\n- [OpenAI Adapter](../adapters/openai) -- Full OpenAI provider options\n"}
